                           Ordinis Cartusien' prope london'</q> (fol. 1r, at foot); s.
                     xv.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Described by <persName>Thomas
                        Hearne</persName> as belonging to Mr <persName role="fmo">John
                        Murray</persName>. It contained a 'Mortuary Bill containing petitions for
                     the souls of some persons'. Hearne, <title>Collections</title>, Oxford
                     Historical Society VII ([1722]), 339, 388, 389. John Murray loaned it to
                     Hearne.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">In the second edition of Medieval Libraries
                     of Great Britain (1964), this book was listed as untraced, but with the
                     following footnote: 'perhaps identical with Harley 6579' (p. 122, n. 4). In
                     MLGB3 (2009-2015), the s. xv inscription was supplied, and the book was listed
                     under Harley MS 6579 rather than as untraced.</provenance>
               </history>
